Replace the ``@base`` filament warning with a vendor-lock check that fires when the resolved ``filament_max_volumetric_speed`` exceeds the ~15 mm³/s ceiling a generic hotend can sustain — catching the real failure mode (under-extrusion from feeding generic filament through a vendor-tuned profile). Also: wizard now defaults to "Generic ..." filaments unless the user opts into vendor-branded options, and the AI setup prompt + docs are updated to recommend matching the filament profile to the actual filament loaded rather than the printer brand.
